        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/4bbf92/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2017-12-21T04:41:39.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>So since I can't do hard statstics but can write code... I wrote a little app to roll dice and show me the results.&nbsp; One interesting thing is just how often a fairly decent dice set d8,d8,d8 succeeds cleanly only 4 percent of the time.&nbsp; It makes it clear that boosts are your friend.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Here are the results of a 8d,8d,8d. The values for overcome and boosts are the percentage chance of getting that value, the Attack/Defend results is the average value you would roll. (With either Min,Mid, or Max)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Oh and devs.. if these look wrong, let me know. I might have made a typo somewhere. ;)</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
